Figure 6:Qualitative comparison on FLUX.2-klein-4B: BF16 vs. MACaQ
(MXFP4 W4A4) vs. the official NVFP4 checkpoint, scaled to 512 pix width. Same seed per prompt. The inset number shows the lpips (lower is better). For a quantitative comparison see Table3.(a) Photographic prompts:(1) a photorealistic portrait of an elderly fisherman, weathered face, golden hour light;
(2) an astronaut riding a horse on the moon, earth in the background, dramatic;
(3) a cozy bookshop interior, warm lamps, stacks of old books, cat sleeping on a chair;
(4) a futuristic city skyline at dusk, flying cars, volumetric clouds, highly detailed;
(5) a corgi wearing tiny sunglasses on a tropical beach, vibrant colors;
(6) a macro photograph of a dewdrop on a spider web at sunrise.(b) GenEval2 prompts:(1) four brown monkeys;
(2) a blue kangaroo and a cookie;
(3) a stone guitar and a plastic lion;
(4) two purple flowers in front of three dogs;
(5) a bicycle to the left of a rabbit, and five brown turtles;
(6) three purple giraffes to the left of two pink guitars, and two suitcases.
Best viewed zoomed in.
